# catalogues-service

Product catalogue (categories, product classes, options, products, images,
recommendations). Schema follows `catalogue_product_erd.webp`; baskets, orders,
stock, reviews, wishlists and analytics tables in that diagram belong to other
services and are not modelled here.

## Architecture (hexagonal, wired with uber-go/fx)

```
cmd/main.go                       fx.New(infrastructure.Module).Run()
config/                           environment configuration
internal/
  domain/
    model/                        entities and domain errors (no dependencies)
    port/driving.go               what the outside calls   (CategoryService, ProductService, ...)
    port/driven.go                what the core needs      (CategoryRepository, ProductRepository, ...)
  application/                    use cases: implement driving ports, use driven ports
  adapter/
    primary/httpapi/              REST -> driving ports
    secondary/repository/         GORM/Postgres -> driven ports (entities live here)
  infrastructure/
    database/                     connection + auto-migration
    server/                       HTTP server + fx lifecycle
    module.go                     composes every fx module
```

Dependencies point inwards: adapters import `domain`, never the other way.
`infrastructure/module_test.go` validates the whole fx graph without a database.

## API

| Resource | Routes |
|---|---|
| Categories | `POST/GET /v1/categories`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /v1/categories/{id}` |
| Product classes | `POST/GET /v1/product-classes`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /v1/product-classes/{id}` |
| Options | `POST/GET /v1/options`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /v1/options/{id}` |
| Products | `POST/GET /v1/products`, `GET/PUT/DELETE /v1/products/{id}` |
| Images | `POST /v1/products/{id}/images`, `DELETE /v1/products/{id}/images/{image_id}` |
| Recommendations | `PUT /v1/products/{id}/recommendations` (replaces the list) |
| Health | `GET /health` |

`GET /v1/products` accepts `category_id`, `q` (title or UPC), `public=true`,
`limit` (default 50, max 200) and `offset`.

There is no authentication in this service; run it behind the gateway.

## Run

```
cp .env.example .env
go run ./cmd
```
